1. Definitions

"Software" means the source code, documentation and other files published in
the Nekotia repository, and any part of them.

"Build" means any compiled, linked, packaged or otherwise generated form of the
Software or of a Derivative Work (for example a kernel image, an ISO image, a
disk image or an executable program).

"Derivative Work" means any work that contains, is based on, or is modified
from the Software or a part of it.

"Corresponding Source" for a Build means the complete source code of the
Software and of all changes and additions used to produce it, together with the
scripts and instructions needed to build it.

"Licensor" means the copyright holder named above and the contributors to the
Software, each for their own contributions.

"You" means any person or organization exercising rights under this license.

"Commercial Purpose" means any use intended for, or directed toward, commercial
advantage or monetary compensation, including: selling, renting or licensing
the Software, a Build or a Derivative Work; charging for access to them, for
their distribution, hosting or support, or for services built on them; including
them in a product, device, service or offering that is sold or monetized in any
way, including through advertising; and using them in the course of the business
of a for-profit organization. Personal use, study, research, teaching, hobby
projects, and use by nonprofit, educational or public organizations for their
noncommercial activities are not Commercial Purposes.

